        "created_at": "2015-05-18T19:09:46.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"cnranger\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/53a042/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> cnranger:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>That's Awesome, my 6 year old son has been able to grasp the game despite not being able to read yet, he has his favourite characters and knows what their cards do (currently Ra and Captain Cosmic).</p>\n<p>On Saturday after much asking I finally got my beloved wife to try the game after she suggested playing Pandemic, her response was, \"I'm not going to like it but if you really want to I'll play it.\" She had seen in partially played with cards and tokens everywhere and I think that had given her a bad impression.</p>\n<p>After the first game against Baron Blade in Megapolis she said \"I'm not sure if I like it, I think we'll need to try it again tomorrow.\" A loss to Infinitor and a win against Voss later and she says \"I might maybe like this game just a little bit\" and ended the night with a win against Plague Rat and a loss to the Dreamer.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>It's awesome she was willing to give it a try! But yeah, I've been impessed by how the game can easily hook hard-core gamers and casual gamers, alike.&nbsp;</p>",
